{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785352825894946002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"unrelative-inbred-piglet","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"b9386ec4396f1993c813e12882d465207aaabd024ecdf1ac46219f59d10cd949","event_uuid":"ee4fd2bb-676e-4950-882d-bc8634cf0c56","position":{"commit_sha":"8e87589124468cb37c2e57a3ff613373e7a9b8a0","position":"1785352804914422001-ee4fd2bb-676e-4950-882d-bc8634cf0c56"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"40537dbd553b58efb3f7337851d7c8bdb3ac65bc0aa2fb371af068a836343cdd","event_uuid":"504d2b5a-e5ea-4d63-9f7c-7f67e36b6aa7","position":{"commit_sha":"2a0b44a9e57ab76620a947e66e2972a9e8c5d95a","position":"1785352815832080001-504d2b5a-e5ea-4d63-9f7c-7f67e36b6aa7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"dcfa875629c41c6cbeecf1878325648367f46a865e2db1addc6584691b01b9aa","event_uuid":"438924f4-9611-4d2b-a8f8-aa662ba18b3c","position":{"commit_sha":"4c782e507acaa557ebcbdb8e9ee7d2b9afbfbee3","position":"1785352825894946001-438924f4-9611-4d2b-a8f8-aa662ba18b3c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1785352804914422001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"438924f4-9611-4d2b-a8f8-aa662ba18b3c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"0a94-e104-7304-4d85"}],"description":"## Symptom\n\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ.py` fails with\n\n    AssertionError: assert False\n      where False = isinstance(Mutation(direction=..., action=..., target='DSO-42', ...),\n                               <class 'mutation.Mutation'>)\n\ni.e. an object that IS a `Mutation` fails `isinstance` against `Mutation`. Observed on\n`macos-latest / py3.13` in CI while `ubuntu-latest / py3.13` — same Python version — passed, which is the\nsignature of a collection-order dependency rather than a version or logic defect.\n\n## Root cause (reproduced deterministically, not inferred)\n\nFive test files load `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mutation.py` **by path** under the SHARED\n`sys.modules` key `\"mutation\"`:\n\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ.py`\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_conflict_resolution.py`\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_quarantine_suppression.py`\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_emits_probe.py`\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_mutation.py`\n\nThree of them shared this helper:\n\n    def _load_module(name: str, path: Path) -> ModuleType:\n        spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(name, path)\n        mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n        sys.modules.setdefault(name, mod)   # keeps an EARLIER registration\n        spec.loader.exec_module(mod)\n        return mod                          # ...but returns the NEW module\n\n`setdefault` keeps whatever was registered first, yet the function returns the freshly-created module. So\nwhenever another file has already registered `\"mutation\"`, the fixture hands back a module object that is\n**not** `sys.modules[\"mutation\"]` — two live copies of the same source, with two distinct `Mutation` classes.\n\nMeanwhile `differ._load_mutation()` resolves its `Mutation` cache-first out of `sys.modules` (checking\n`\"mutation\"`, `\"rebar_reconciler.mutation\"`, …). So the differ builds objects from copy A while the test\nasserts against copy B, and `isinstance` is correctly `False`.\n\nWhichever file pytest collects first wins the `setdefault`, so the outcome depends on collection order —\nwhich differs between macOS and Linux.\n\n**Deterministic reproduction** (fails before the fix, passes after):\n\n    pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_conflict_resolution.py \\\n           tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ.py -q\n\nThe natural alphabetical order puts `test_differ.py` first, so it normally wins and the suite is green; that\nis why this sat latent.\n\n## Fix (landed with story J4, `0a94-e104-7304-4d85`)\n\nMake the helper cache-first, so the returned module always IS the registered one — mirroring what\n`differ._load_mutation()` already does:\n\n    cached = sys.modules.get(name)\n    if cached is not None and getattr(cached, \"__file__\", None) == str(path):\n        return cached\n    ...\n    sys.modules[name] = mod\n\nApplied to the three `setdefault`-based helpers. `test_differ_emits_probe.py` already assigned\nunconditionally (self-consistent) and `test_mutation.py` loads inline, so neither carried the defect.\n\n## Why it was bundled with J4 rather than landed separately\n\nJ4 added two test files, which perturbed macOS collection order enough to make another registrant win the\nrace — turning a latent landmine into a `Verified -1` that blocked J4's own change. The fix therefore had to\nsit at or below J4 in the review stack for J4 to go green. It is test-only, ~6 lines across three files, and\nthe alternative (a separate change spliced beneath an already-pushed one, blocking on its own plan review)\nbought nothing. The bundling is disclosed in J4's commit message rather than smuggled.\n\n## Remaining work this ticket tracks\n\n- [ ] Consider a shared conftest helper so the by-path loader exists ONCE instead of being copy-pasted into\n      five test modules — the duplication is what let three copies carry the same defect\n- [ ] Audit the other shared by-path `sys.modules` keys (`differ`, `config`, `adf`, `outbound_fields`,\n      `comment_limits`) for the same `setdefault`-then-return-new shape\n- [ ] Consider making CI run the suite in a randomized order (e.g. `pytest-randomly`) so order-dependent\n      coupling fails fast and locally rather than as a platform-specific surprise","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ.py","reason":"cache-first loader so the returned module is the registered one"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_conflict_resolution.py","reason":"same setdefault-then-return-new defect"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_quarantine_suppression.py","reason":"same setdefault-then-return-new defect"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2bc7-d77b-641c-42aa","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Test helpers return an unregistered copy of mutation.py, so isinstance fails on a collection-order flip","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ee4fd2bb-676e-4950-882d-bc8634cf0c56","504d2b5a-e5ea-4d63-9f7c-7f67e36b6aa7","438924f4-9611-4d2b-a8f8-aa662ba18b3c"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785352825894946002,"uuid":"00ed2043-667b-4275-af1c-2d00c383c449"}